From: Stained Glass OS contributors
Subject: winex11: a window focused before it is shown gets the keyboard

Firefox gives its top-level window the focus and then shows it. On the
shell's desktop (no window manager), winex11 asks X for the focus when
Win32 focus changes; X refuses it for a window not yet on the screen, and
on MapNotify winex11 asked again only if the focus was on a child of the
window -- IsChild is false for the window itself. X kept the keyboard on
the window that had it (the desktop's), and typing into Firefox did nothing
until focus moved away and back (opening Start, minimizing).

Gate: test/focusmap-gate.sh (make test-focusmap).
---
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
@@ -1027,7 +1027,13 @@
     if (!data->managed && !data->embedded && data->desired_state.wm_state != WithdrawnState)
     {
         HWND hwndFocus = get_focus();
-        if (hwndFocus && NtUserIsChild( hwnd, hwndFocus ))
+        /* Stained Glass OS: the window itself too. A program that gives its
+         * top-level window the focus before showing it (Firefox) had its
+         * X focus request refused -- the window was not mapped yet -- and it
+         * was never made again: X kept the keyboard on the window that had it
+         * (the desktop's), and typing went nowhere until focus moved away and
+         * back. IsChild is false for the window itself. */
+        if (hwndFocus && (hwndFocus == hwnd || NtUserIsChild( hwnd, hwndFocus )))
             set_input_focus( data );
     }
     release_win_data( data );
